1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,020
Do it first. The rest of the day feels lighter, not because you did more, but because you stopped

2
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:06,420
carrying the thing that weighed the most. Here is something that's changed how I measure a day.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:12,900
Instead of only tracking what is left on the 2-2 list, I write by hand the 5 or 6 most meaningful

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:19,700
things I actually did. Not everything. The things that moved something forward. 2-2 lists create

5
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:26,580
a permanent state of deficit. The list never goes to zero. You end the day and all you see is

6
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:33,300
what you did not finish. The done list corrects your perception of yourself. We consistently

7
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:39,700
underestimate how much we accomplish in a day. Over time, it builds an accurate picture of your

8
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:47,540
real capacity, which makes planning more realistic and breaks the cycle of punishing over commitment.

9
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:48,200
The fifth habit is one 90-minute block of deep work per day. Not Pomodoro's 90 minutes.
